{"parentUuid":"cd16dfc8-6991-402e-b3d7-0208974a4d70","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Xk37ajU4vquVF4FQinF1hx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Looking over PR #1076 \"Add user-defined redaction rules and rule packs\" (currently REVIEW_REQUIRED, all CI green).\n\n## Verdict\n\nLooks good to ship. Architecture is clean, error paths are warn-and-skip (right call for a security feature — one bad rule shouldn't silence the rest), and test coverage is thorough. A few comments below — none are blockers.\n\n## Strengths\n\n- **Two surfaces, one engine.** Inline `custom_redactions` and pack files feed the same compiled-rule list; the layered split in `redact.String()` is a one-liner add (layer 5) — minimal risk to existing detectors.\n- **Warn-and-skip across the board.** Invalid regex, missing dir, unreadable file, symlink, schema error, sample mismatch — none are fatal. The settings-load and pack-walk paths cannot kill redaction.\n- **Strict schema parsing.** `DisallowUnknownFields` on JSON, `KnownFields(true)` on YAML, *and* an extra `Decode(&extra)` to reject trailing content / multi-doc YAML. Good belt-and-suspenders.\n- **Per-key local override semantics** (`mergeRedaction`) are correct and tested at the merge layer (`TestLoadMerged_CustomRedactionsPerKeyOverride`).\n- **`redactors/local/`** convention + `.entire/.gitignore` integration is a nice UX touch for personal rules.\n- **Privacy-aware logging.** `REDACTED` is a great regression guard — sample inputs are summarized by `sample_index` + `sample_length`, never raw.\n\n## Things worth a second look\n\n1. **`paths.AbsPath` failure fallback walks CWD** — `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go:380-386`. If `WorktreeRoot` fails (e.g., process started outside a repo, but settings somehow loaded), `packsDir` falls back to the relative `.entire/redactors`. `LoadPacks` then walks that path relative to CWD, which can pick up an unrelated `.entire/redactors/` if someone happened to be in a directory that has one. Low likelihood, but the safer move is to skip pack-loading entirely on `paths.AbsPath` failure. Optional.\n\n2. **No guard against over-broad regex (e.g. `.*`, `(.+)`).** A user-supplied `.*` would redact every transcript. Sample-validation catches this only if they wrote samples. Consider either (a) a doc warning under \"Customizing redaction\" that an unanchored permissive regex will eat everything, or (b) rejecting patterns that match the empty string at compile time. Doc fix is enough IMO.\n\n3. **No de-duplication across packs.** `validatePack` rejects duplicate rule IDs *within* a pack, but two packs can both define `id: api-key`. Behavior is correct (both run, both labels stay distinct via `pack.Name+\".\"+rule.ID`), but if two packs happen to have the same `name` (e.g., one in root + one in `local/`), the labels collide in logs. Worth a one-liner check in `LoadPacks` to warn on duplicate pack names, or just document it.\n\n4. **Filename-stem-must-match-pack-name** is enforced (`packs.go:107`). Justification is good (consistent logs/discovery), but it's a UX papercut on rename and isn't documented in `docs/security-and-privacy.md`. Add one line to the \"Required fields\" section: \"`name` must equal the filename stem (e.g., `acme-internal.yaml` → `acme-internal`)\" — actually you already have this. Nevermind, good.\n\n5. **Per-call linear scan.** `detectCustomRules` runs `FindAllStringIndex` per rule per `String()` call. Fine for tens of rules; with hundreds of pack rules and high-frequency transcript scanning, worth keeping in mind. Not a today-problem.\n\n6. **Minor test gap:** symlinked *subdirectory* (vs. symlinked file) isn't covered. `WalkDir` won't follow them by default, and `d.Type()&fs.ModeSymlink` will skip them, but a one-line test would lock the behavior in.\n\n7. **`Pack.Description` / `Rule.Description`** are accepted by the schema but never surfaced anywhere (no logs, no `entire doctor`). Fine to keep as human-readability fields, but a comment to that effect on the struct would prevent \"why isn't this shown?\" issues later.\n\n## Nits\n\n- `EnsureRedactionConfigured` is wrapped in `sync.Once`, which means rule edits require a process restart. That's the right model, but it's not in the docs — worth one line under \"Troubleshooting\" (\"rule changes take effect on the next CLI invocation\"). You already have something close (\"The rule reloads on the next CLI invocation\") under \"disable a rule temporarily\" — maybe make it general.\n- `redact/custom.go:25` — `label` on `compiledCustomRule` is never read at redact time (regions are emitted with empty label). Comment already says this; could simplify by dropping the field entirely and only keeping it in log-emission scope. Cosmetic.\n\nHappy to push fixes for any of these if you want — say the word."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1569,"cache_read_input_tokens":96521,"output_tokens":5102,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1569,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":5102,"cache_read_input_tokens":96521,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1569,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1569},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaxeU1mgH5Lq85DCrisx5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d55dc48b-9033-4b08-86cd-91f2c8f907f1","timestamp":"2026-05-12T12:08:05.290Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"13e26df4-5885-4c44-9469-8449e56488e6","version":"2.1.129","gitBranch":"feat/redaction-rule-extensions"}
