{"parentUuid":"eb3ef013-8d6b-4899-b311-44879600d780","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"23a4b2cd-c9ec-4ee6-8399-f284a0fae7e5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S1xpUiw2vNaWEjxnC3Aciq","type":"tool_result","content":"190\t- Internal service tokens (`ACME_*`, `INTERNAL_*`) and custom env-var prefixes the bundled detectors don't know about.\n191\t- Project-specific session formats.\n192\t- Project codenames or other identifiers you don't want stored in transcripts.\n193\t- Specific words or phrases you'd rather keep out of session archives.\n194\t\n195\tFile an issue when the rule would benefit every Entire user (e.g., a major SaaS issued a new token format), when a built-in is producing false positives on common idioms in your codebase, or when a built-in is *not* catching a well-known shared format (we'd rather fix the built-in than have everyone ship the same custom rule).\n196\t\n197\t### Troubleshooting\n198\t\n199\t- **My rule doesn't redact anything.** Warnings about invalid patterns or sample mismatches appear on stderr when Entire initializes redaction, such as hooks that write checkpoints or `entire doctor`. Look for lines mentioning your label or pack path.\n200\t- **My pack file is silently ignored.** Filenames must end in `.yaml`, `.yml`, or `.json`. Other extensions are skipped.\n201\t- **I want to disable a rule temporarily.** Comment it out (prefix the YAML key with `#`) or remove the entry from `custom_redactions`. The rule reloads on the next CLI invocation.\n202\t\n203\t## Limitations\n204\t\n205\t- **Best-effort.** Novel or low-entropy secrets (short passwords, predictable tokens) may not be caught.\n206\t- **Filenames and binary data.** Secrets in filenames, binary files, or deeply nested structures may not be detected.\n207\t- **JSONL skip rules.** Entire skips scanning fields named `signature`, fields ending in `id`/`ids`, structural-path fields (`filepath`, `file_path`, `cwd`, `root`, `directory`, `dir`, `path`), and objects whose `type` starts with `image` or equals `base64` — all to avoid false positives.\n208\t- **Custom PII patterns are user-authored.** Teams own the correctness of their `custom_patterns`. An invalid regex is logged and skipped, not enforced.\n209\t- **Users are ultimately responsible** for reviewing what they commit and push. Redaction is a safety net, not a guarantee.\n210\t\n211\t## Telemetry\n212\t\n213\tThe CLI captures anonymous usage analytics by default. Sent to PostHog with `DisableGeoIP` enabled. Captured per command: command name, selected agent, whether Entire is enabled in the repo, CLI version, OS/arch, and **names** of flags passed (never their values). The distinct ID is a hashed machine identifier (`machineid.ProtectedID`), not a user identity.\n214\t"}]},"uuid":"cdf07a6b-e9e6-40c9-9fb4-b25879e097fb","timestamp":"2026-05-12T12:17:10.045Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/docs/security-and-privacy.md","content":"- Internal service tokens (`ACME_*`, `INTERNAL_*`) and custom env-var prefixes the bundled detectors don't know about.\n- Project-specific session formats.\n- Project codenames or other identifiers you don't want stored in transcripts.\n- Specific words or phrases you'd rather keep out of session archives.\n\nFile an issue when the rule would benefit every Entire user (e.g., a major SaaS issued a new token format), when a built-in is producing false positives on common idioms in your codebase, or when a built-in is *not* catching a well-known shared format (we'd rather fix the built-in than have everyone ship the same custom rule).\n\n### Troubleshooting\n\n- **My rule doesn't redact anything.** Warnings about invalid patterns or sample mismatches appear on stderr when Entire initializes redaction, such as hooks that write checkpoints or `entire doctor`. Look for lines mentioning your label or pack path.\n- **My pack file is silently ignored.** Filenames must end in `.yaml`, `.yml`, or `.json`. Other extensions are skipped.\n- **I want to disable a rule temporarily.** Comment it out (prefix the YAML key with `#`) or remove the entry from `custom_redactions`. The rule reloads on the next CLI invocation.\n\n## Limitations\n\n- **Best-effort.** Novel or low-entropy secrets (short passwords, predictable tokens) may not be caught.\n- **Filenames and binary data.** Secrets in filenames, binary files, or deeply nested structures may not be detected.\n- **JSONL skip rules.** Entire skips scanning fields named `signature`, fields ending in `id`/`ids`, structural-path fields (`filepath`, `file_path`, `cwd`, `root`, `directory`, `dir`, `path`), and objects whose `type` starts with `image` or equals `base64` — all to avoid false positives.\n- **Custom PII patterns are user-authored.** Teams own the correctness of their `custom_patterns`. An invalid regex is logged and skipped, not enforced.\n- **Users are ultimately responsible** for reviewing what they commit and push. Redaction is a safety net, not a guarantee.\n\n## Telemetry\n\nThe CLI captures anonymous usage analytics by default. Sent to PostHog with `DisableGeoIP` enabled. Captured per command: command name, selected agent, whether Entire is enabled in the repo, CLI version, OS/arch, and **names** of flags passed (never their values). The distinct ID is a hashed machine identifier (`machineid.ProtectedID`), not a user identity.\n","numLines":25,"startLine":190,"totalLines":231}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"eb3ef013-8d6b-4899-b311-44879600d780","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"13e26df4-5885-4c44-9469-8449e56488e6","version":"2.1.129","gitBranch":"feat/redaction-rule-extensions"}
